WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
- Hi.
- This is a cute dress, too!

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.783
- Thank you, thank you.

00:00:02.783 --> 00:00:04.120
I actually busted the belt,

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.890
so we just had to sew it in the car,

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:07.723
(Kelly laughs)
but we're here,

00:00:07.723 --> 00:00:09.580
we're doing it, thank you.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.840
- Meet Tinashe, meet Jeff.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.429
- Hi, guys.
(audience applauding)

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:15.080
- So Jeff's family named him Chex Mix,

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.360
so how did you get the name Tinx?

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.160
- So when I was younger, I
actually wasn't that confident.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.720
And so I watched this movie
and there was a character

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.230
in this movie called "All I
Wanna Do" called Tinka Parker,

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.380
and she was like the coolest girl.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.947
And I told my friends, I was like,

00:00:28.947 --> 00:00:31.171
"Guys, I have an alter ego now.

00:00:31.171 --> 00:00:32.200
Her name is Tinka Parker."

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.120
And when I'm her, I'm confident,
and I'm cool and whatever.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.170
And slowly, I just started
to become more confident,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.820
and slowly, they just started
to call me Tinka Parker,

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.400
then Tinka, then Tinx.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.530
So I've been called Tinx
for like 20 years now.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.363
- That's cute.

00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:46.196
- Yeah, yeah.
(audience claps)

00:00:46.196 --> 00:00:48.300
It's like my Sasha Fierce moment.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.210
We all need a nickname, an alter ego.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.043
- It is funny,

00:00:52.043 --> 00:00:53.550
I don't know if y'all feel
this when you're on stage,

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.910
but I do feel different,

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.150
and I do feel more bold and confident.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.360
Do you feel like that
when you're on stage?

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.193
- Absolutely.

00:00:58.193 --> 00:01:00.390
There's this part of me, I call her Nashe,

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.397
I just drop the first syllable of my name.

00:01:02.397 --> 00:01:04.940
(audience cheers)
She is this super confident,

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.850
it's weird 'cause it lives
inside of you already,

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.850
but it gives the opportunity
to feel like you can kind of-

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.483
- Absolutely.
- Step into that.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.793
- Do you feel like that
on stage, more confident?

00:01:13.793 --> 00:01:16.860
- I just, yeah, I just feel
like I'm talking to my friends,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.610
so I look forward to it.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.130
- Oh, I think that's why
people love you though, too,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.340
'cause you're so relatable in that sense.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.660
It's conversational.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.493
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:23.493 --> 00:01:25.670
Everybody loves everybody here.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:27.980
So wait, so you've got millions
of followers on social.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.670
So how did this all start for you?

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.350
- So it started in quarantine.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:35.690
I downloaded TikTok to try to stay sane,

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.680
and I just, I kind of
was like at rock bottom,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.670
as we all were, going out of our minds.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:41.503
And I was like "You know what?

00:01:41.503 --> 00:01:42.336
I don't care anymore.

00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:43.370
I'm just gonna to try this.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.210
I'm just gonna make a video."

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.607
And as soon as I made my
first TikTok, I was like,

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.390
"This is what I'm supposed to
do with the rest of my life."

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.140
I wanna entertain people.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.300
I wanna connect with people.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.630
I wanna make videos,
and the rest is history.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.463
- You're very funny.

00:01:54.463 --> 00:01:55.641
And the one-
- Wow.

00:01:55.641 --> 00:01:56.890
(audience cheers)
- One of the videos,

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.037
it's hilarious, 'cause you're like,

00:01:58.037 --> 00:02:00.900
"So it was my daily cry during pandemic,"

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.303
'cause everybody did have
their daily moment of like-

00:02:02.303 --> 00:02:03.700
- We have your daily cry.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.480
You gotta put it in the
schedule right between-

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.313
- But it was so dry-

00:02:06.313 --> 00:02:07.800
- Organizing sweatpants-
- Your wit.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.310
- And eating rotisserie chicken,

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.452
standing up in your kitchen.

00:02:10.452 --> 00:02:12.412
It was a busy time for everybody.

00:02:12.412 --> 00:02:13.300
- You don't have time to sit down.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.160
You've all the time to
sit down, but we're not.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.830
So wait, so you're known as
the big sister of TikTok.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.480
So when did people start
to come to you for advice?

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.370
'Cause I love that.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.780
- It was honestly pretty
immediate, and it's great.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:26.090
And I think that I love to ask for advice,

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.100
and I think it's two
sides of the same coin.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.290
I love to ask it, I love to give it.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.320
It's all about sharing information.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.270
And if I can pass on a tip to another girl

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.490
and save her a little
bit of time or angst,

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.450
that's a win.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.470
That's what life is about.
(audience claps)

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.491
- I'm not gonna lie.

00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:43.990
I've definitely seen some of your TikToks

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.630
going through it in 2020,

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.790
and been like, that was some
real stuff that she said.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.362
- I cried a lot on the internet
in the past year and a half.

00:02:52.362 --> 00:02:53.450
- [Tinashe] Yeah, but it helped.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.080
- Yeah, I had a really bad breakup.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.340
And I made a video, and I
was like, I got cheated on,

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.250
and I made a video saying
I'm not embarrassed

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.310
that I fell in love and trusted someone.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.790
And I put it out there.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:05.623
I was like, why not?

00:03:05.623 --> 00:03:07.647
And I got so many
messages of girls saying,

00:03:07.647 --> 00:03:09.670
"This helped me," "We've all been there."

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:10.810
- We've all been there.
- "It's a bad time,

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.670
but we've all been there."

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.503
- And it's so true.

00:03:12.503 --> 00:03:13.940
For some reason, women or men,

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:14.900
I know guys have been cheated on too,

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.100
everybody goes to like,
"What did I do wrong?"

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:17.933
or "Why would they do that?"

00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:20.080
And it's like, "Wait, what?"
- Yeah, exactly.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.340
It's not about you.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.620
It's about the other person.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:23.870
It's not embarrassing.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.210
It's just, you got your heart stomped on.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.043
- Yeah.

00:03:27.043 --> 00:03:28.320
I like being open like that.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.098
My mother is always shocked.

00:03:30.098 --> 00:03:32.130
(audience laughing)
But whatever.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:35.000
So wait, your new podcast
is called "It's Me, Tinx."

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.760
So do you give advice on the podcast too?

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:37.740
Is that how it came-
- I do.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.320
I give advice on the podcast.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.720
We talk about literally everything.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.760
As you were saying, I love to be open.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.380
And I also have a radio show

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.580
every Wednesday that's live call-in.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.880
So people can call in and ask me-

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:48.900
- That's Sirius, right, on XM?

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.060
- On SiriusXM Stars, yeah, channel 109.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.150
And it's just so fun.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.680
I had my first one yesterday.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.930
And to hear my followers' voices

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.860
and to just talk through
problems with them,

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.500
it was the best feeling in the world.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.380
- Especially for someone,
I love conversation,

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.690
and I love learning and
progressing, so it's perfect.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.690
What a great job-
- It's really fun.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:07.523
- For somebody that loves that.

00:04:07.523 --> 00:04:09.190
- Thank you, thank you.
- That's so cool.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.730
Okay, it's time for another little break.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.410
You can listen to Tinx's new
podcast, "It's Me, Tinx,"

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.910
wherever you get your podcast.

